{
  "schema": "richos-mobile-perf-benchmarks/1",
  "about": "The best p95 RichConnect has measured per device class for cold launch and warm resume. `perf.py compare` and every record `perf.py android|ios|merge` writes are judged against it; a p95 over benchmark x (1 + allowancePercent/100) is SLOWER and refused (exit 4). Numbers change only through `perf.py benchmark-update` and a commit of this file. Records named here are private (richos-hq or the external SSD); this file holds no serials, UDIDs, samples or traces.",
  "noiseRule": "allowancePercent = median, over the class's noiseSeries, of twoRunBoundPercent = 100 x 1.96 x sqrt(2) x bootstrapSeMs / p95Ms, where bootstrapSeMs is the standard deviation of the nearest-rank p95 over 2000 resamples (seed 95) of that series' own samples (benchmark.py p95_noise)",
